1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared heading scanner and Section Map model[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]model[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]model: refactor the section-header scanner into one walker that the keys[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the map share, then add the pure Section Map model (labels, nesting [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]depth, windowing, chips, counter, aria sentence) with unit and parity [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]property tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Section Map card painter, placement, and styles[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]card[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]card: build the pure DOM painter with keyed in-place reconciliation, the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]margin/overlay/compact placement function, the .bob-section-map styles, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and a headless-Chromium preview whose screenshots are reviewed against [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the visual spec.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Jump integration, lifecycle controller, landing flash, and [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]peek[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]wiring[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model, card[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]wiring: move the section jump into a new fragment, fix the double [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scroll, add the landing flash, the hold/linger/fade lifecycle with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]activity dismissal, the doc-keyed heading cache, the aria-live sentence,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the unbound peek command.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Real-Obsidian acceptance, docs, and deploy[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ship[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wiring[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ship: prove the map end to end in real Obsidian over CDP (both key [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]routes, lifecycle, dismissal, wrap, windowing, compact, unchanged note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bytes), document it in the navigation plugin reference, and deploy with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob plugins sync.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-rc","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-rc.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"bob-cli-rc.1"},"source_run_id":"run-f7c98424bd6687cb19eea1f5c073f547","started_at":"2026-11-27T20:08:34.377234+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rc","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rc.1","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rc.2","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rc.3","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rc.4","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-rc.land"]}
